# Terminal shell backend (system shell vs Wawona PTY)

| Product | Backend |
|---|---|
| macOS, Linux | **System shell**: user's login shell `-l`, real pty |
| iOS / iPadOS Mode B (TrollStore, Sileo) | **System shell**: jailbreak / bootstrap login shell |
| Android Mode B (root, outside Play) | **System shell** |
| iOS / iPadOS / tvOS / watchOS / visionOS Mode A, Android Play | **Wawona PTY shell**: in-process `wawona_zsh_main` + `wwn_pty`, no fork/exec |

- Rust `domain::terminal_shell` decides. Hosts never hardcode the shell.
- Rust Terminal (libghostty-rs) is the grid on both. System shell: Rust opens
  a real pty and spawns the resolved login shell. Wawona PTY: Rust attaches
  to `wwn_pty`. Nothing spawns a process in Mode A.
- Never a placeholder/demo command in a Terminal tab.
- Mode A artifacts must not contain the system-shell spawn path.

Canonical: `Wawona/docs/agent-rules/wawona-terminal-shell-backend.md`.
